# C047 — @suluk/provision: declarative service provisioning modelled on the Open Service Broker API, driven like
# drizzle-kit. Operator-surfaced ("toolfactory has a lot of LOC in provisioning/setup scripts; hook it up with @suluk/env
# + @suluk/cloudflare + @suluk/deploy + a new @suluk/provision; use the Open Service Broker API" + "heavily inspired by
# the drizzle-kit migrations CLI"). Replaces toolfactory's ~700 LOC of hand-rolled provision*.ts / mint-*.ts /
# sync-secrets.ts. Operator chose: (1) LAYERING = "a layer ABOVE, composing" — provision owns the catalog/lifecycle/CLI,
# the brokers WRAP @suluk/cloudflare's existing provisioners + @suluk/stripe, bindings LAND in @suluk/env; (2) v1 SCOPE =
# "full framework". NOT a contract facet — an app-provisioning library; never touches the matcher (no D1-wall concern).

# THE DESIGN: OSB API gives the LIFECYCLE (catalog -> provision Service Instance -> bind credentials -> deprovision, with
# last-operation polling for async + orphan mitigation); drizzle-kit gives the CLI ergonomics (a declarative config ->
# plan/diff -> apply/push -> pull -> check). The LOAD-BEARING idea = the BINDING CHAIN: provisioning is a DAG where each
# instance's bind OUTPUT feeds the next's params AND the env manifest (create D1 -> bind database_id; mint scoped token ->
# bind CLOUDFLARE_D1_TOKEN; create Stripe webhook -> bind STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET), all landing in @suluk/env (typed +
# post-quantum-encrypted + commit-safe). A param string `@<ref>.<key>` is both a DAG edge and a substitution. Brokers
# grounded in toolfactory's scripts: cloudflare-d1/kv/r2/secrets (wrap @suluk/cloudflare), stripe (provision-stripe.ts),
# domains (the async 229-LOC one), tokens (mint-*.ts). DESIGNED + core built => ceiling 0.5.
claim provision_osb_drizzlekit_design_layer_above: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when provision_osb_drizzlekit_design_layer_above == False

# C047 BUILD #1 — the CORE OSB framework built 2026-07-01 (broker-agnostic; the design-risk layer FIRST). The Broker
# interface (catalog/provision/lastOperation/bind/deprovision — OSB-shaped, the optional verbs let a sync/non-bindable/
# never-torn-down service omit them) + InstanceSpec/InstanceState/ProvisionResult (sync|in-progress, the async ack MAY
# carry outputs) + BindingSink/StateStore seams. defineProvision validates statically (unique refs, acyclic binding DAG).
# refs.ts: parseRef/depsOf/resolveParams (FAIL-CLOSED on a missing producer output) + a stable fingerprint (drift detect).
# dag.ts: topoOrder (Kahn; throws on dup-ref/unknown-ref/cycle) — producers before consumers. plan.ts: the PURE diff
# (desired config x live state -> create/update/noop/deprovision steps in DAG order + orphans, prune-guarded). apply.ts:
# the executor — walk the plan, resolve params from accumulated outputs (the binding chain), provision (idempotent), poll
# lastOperation until an async create settles (clock+sleep INJECTED for determinism), bind, land outputs in the sink,
# deprovision orphans last, save the journal. check.ts: checkDrift/assertNoDrift (the CI gate). memory.ts: in-memory
# store+sink (dry-run/test seams). WITNESSED — provision 10 pass through the FULL lifecycle with mock brokers: DAG order +
# async polling (in-progress->succeeded) + the binding chain (a downstream @ref.key resolving to a freshly provisioned
# database_id) + idempotent re-apply (all-noops, zero provider calls) + param-drift re-provisions ONLY the drifted
# instance + orphan prune deprovisions (and WITHOUT --prune never tears down) + the drift gate. tsc clean. A real bug the
# witness caught + fixed: an async ack that also yields outputs (a D1 uuid known at submit time) must thread them past the
# poll. REMAINING: the concrete brokers (cloudflare-d1/kv/r2/secrets, stripe, domains, tokens) + the @suluk/env sink
# adapter + the file-backed store + the drizzle-kit-style CLI (plan/apply/pull/studio/check) + the toolfactory cutover.
claim provision_core_osb_framework_built_witnessed: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when provision_core_osb_framework_built_witnessed == False

# C047 BUILD #2 — the CLOUDFLARE brokers + the binding sinks built 2026-07-01. brokers/cloudflare.ts: cloudflareD1/Kv/R2/
# Secrets — each a THIN OSB Broker WRAPPING @suluk/cloudflare's already-witnessed idempotent provisioner (provisionD1/
# provisionKvNamespace/provisionR2Bucket/putSecrets), never re-implementing it; constructed with a CloudflareClient (the
# credential seam). Outputs feed the binding chain: d1 -> database_id (+ applyMigrations when params.migrations), kv ->
# namespace_id, r2 -> bucket_name, secrets -> the pushed names (cloudflare-secrets IS sync-secrets.ts as a broker: params
# {script, secrets} -> idempotent secret put). deprovision = the REST DELETE (the destructive op the orphan-prune calls).
# env-sink.ts: envSink — the binding SINK that lands each (output -> env var) through @suluk/env/node setVar (encrypted by
# default = commit-safe; a `plain` predicate marks non-secret ids readable) — this closes the chain into @suluk/env.
# file-store.ts: fileStore — the on-disk journal (.suluk/provision.json; missing -> empty; pretty JSON, PR-reviewable).
# deps += @suluk/cloudflare + @suluk/env. WITNESSED — provision 15 pass (the brokers over a mock CloudflareClient map
# provisioner->output + hit the right DELETE + skip-empty secrets; envSink writes the mapped vars to a temp .env; fileStore
# round-trips + mkdir -p). tsc clean. REMAINING: the stripe/domains(async)/tokens brokers + the drizzle-kit-style CLI
# (plan/apply/pull/studio/check) + the toolfactory cutover.
claim provision_cloudflare_brokers_and_sinks_built: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when provision_cloudflare_brokers_and_sinks_built == False

# C047 BUILD #3 — the drizzle-kit-style CLI built 2026-07-01 (the headline operator ask: "heavily inspired by the
# drizzle-kit migrations CLI"). app.ts: defineProvisionApp — what a provision.config.ts default-exports (the drizzle.config
# analog): config (desired instances) + brokers registry (service id -> executor) + store + sink; validated up front.
# cli.ts: runCli(app, argv) -> {output, exitCode}, PURE of the process (no process.exit / console) so it's unit-testable;
# the verbs mirror drizzle-kit: `plan` (diff desired vs live, +/~/=/- per step + a summary), `apply`/`push` (provision +
# bind + sink, reports what changed), `check` (the CI gate — EXIT 1 on any drift), `status`/`studio` (the live inventory +
# bound outputs). bin/provision.ts: the thin shell — loads provision.config.ts (--config), prints, exits. WITNESSED —
# provision 20 pass: the full drizzle-kit loop (plan-on-fresh lists creates -> apply -> check clean exit0 -> plan in-sync),
# the drift gate (a config name change -> check EXIT 1), status lists bound outputs, apply --prune deprovisions an orphan,
# an unknown command exits 2; PLUS a bin SMOKE (the real executable: loads a temp config, plans, exits 0; unknown exits 2).
# tsc clean. The package is now USABLE end-to-end for Cloudflare infra. REMAINING (thinner + more app-specific follow-ons):
# the async domains broker (the OSB last-operation showcase) + tokens (scoped CF tokens) + stripe brokers; `pull`
# (introspect live -> config); the toolfactory cutover (replace provision.ts/provision-kv/sync-secrets with a config).
claim provision_drizzlekit_cli_built_witnessed: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when provision_drizzlekit_cli_built_witnessed == False

# C047 BUILD #4 — the ASYNC domains broker + the scoped-token broker built 2026-07-01 (completes the generic Cloudflare
# broker set + the async last-operation story with a REAL broker). cloudflareToken (this is mint-service-tokens.ts): mints
# a least-privilege CF API token (POST /accounts/:a/tokens with permission-group policies) — the token VALUE is returned
# only at creation so it rides out as the `token` binding on provision (the framework's noop-on-unchanged never re-mints);
# deprovision revokes by id. cloudflarePagesDomain (the core of provision-domains.ts, the ASYNC showcase): attaching a
# custom hostname is idempotent but the edge cert issues over minutes -> the textbook OSB last-operation flow — provision
# attaches + returns `in progress`, lastOperation polls the Pages domain status until "active". The project+hostname are
# encoded in the instanceId (the OSB operation anchor) so lastOperation+deprovision are self-contained (no params needed);
# the app-specific redirect/DNS policy stays in the app config. WITNESSED — provision 24 pass: the token mint/value-binding/
# revoke; the domain provision->in-progress + lastOperation pending->active; AND a FULL apply integration where the
# framework polls a real broker's cert to active then lands the url binding (BASE_URL) in the sink. tsc clean. The generic
# Cloudflare broker set is now COMPLETE (d1/kv/r2/secrets/token/pages-domain). REMAINING: the stripe broker (cross-provider;
# best built WITH the cutover since which products/webhooks is app-specific), `pull` (introspect live -> config), and the
# toolfactory cutover (replace provision.ts/provision-kv/provision-domains/mint-*/sync-secrets with a provision.config.ts).
claim provision_async_domains_and_token_brokers_built: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when provision_async_domains_and_token_brokers_built == False

# C047 BUILD #5 — the CAREFUL features built 2026-07-01 (operator: "add more features like pull and even more careful
# features like teardown etc"). pull.ts: `pull` — introspection over OSB "Fetching a Service Instance" (Broker.fetch): plan
# compares config vs the JOURNAL, pull compares the journal vs the PROVIDER, catching EXTERNAL drift (a db dropped in the
# dashboard = missing; an id changed = drifted; no fetch = unknown). `reconcile` folds it back (drop externally-deleted so
# next apply re-creates; MERGE live outputs over drifted, never dropping a bound token the provider can't see). `discover`
# (Broker.list) finds untracked live resources to adopt. teardown.ts: `teardown` — the destructive op: deprovision the
# WHOLE journal CONSUMERS-FIRST (reverse journal order, so a producer isn't removed under a live consumer), async-aware
# (polls). RAILS: a `protected` instance (InstanceSpec+InstanceState gained the flag; prune already skips it) is KEPT
# unless `force`; a no-deprovision broker is kept; `dryRun` previews touching no provider + not saving. CLI: `pull`
# (+--reconcile) + `teardown` GATED behind confirmation (bare teardown = DRY RUN, --yes destroys, --force includes
# protected). Shared poll.ts extracted (apply+teardown). Added Broker.fetch/list + cloudflareD1.fetch/list (the real
# introspection example). WITNESSED — provision 32 pass: pull live/missing/drifted/unknown + reconcile drop+merge +
# discover; teardown reverse-order + dryRun-no-touch + protected-kept-unless-force; a protected orphan kept under prune;
# the CLI teardown dry-run/--yes/--force gate + pull-clean. tsc clean. REMAINING: the SNAPSHOT+MIGRATION model (operator's
# next ask — repeatable/documentable steps like drizzle: generate a migration + snapshot, migrate applies pending in
# order), the stripe broker, + the toolfactory cutover.
claim provision_pull_teardown_protected_careful_features_built: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when provision_pull_teardown_protected_careful_features_built == False

# C047 BUILD #6 — the SNAPSHOT + MIGRATION model built 2026-07-01 (operator: "repeatable documentable steps the way
# drizzle does with snapshots and sql migrations"). The drizzle-kit generate/migrate model for infra, complementing the
# ad-hoc apply/push. snapshot.ts: Snapshot = the point-in-time DESIRED state (config instances) at a migration idx +
# EMPTY_SNAPSHOT baseline. migration.ts: Migration = the DELTA as ordered human-readable steps; diffSnapshots(prev, next)
# — creates/updates in binding-DAG order, deprovisions of dropped instances in reverse (consumers-first). migration-store.
# ts: MigrationStore (memory + FILE impls) — the drizzle on-disk shape: committed meta/_journal.json + NNNN_tag.json (the
# delta) + meta/NNNN_snapshot.json + env-local meta/_applied.json (which migrations THIS env ran, like __drizzle_migrations;
# gitignore). generate.ts: `generate` — diff last snapshot vs config; if changed, write the next migration+snapshot (PURE
# of any provider — records intent, reviewable in a PR); null when unchanged. migrate.ts: `migrate` — run PENDING
# migrations (not in the applied-ledger) in idx order, each REPLAYED by applying its snapshot via apply (pruneOrphans so a
# migration's deprovision runs; protected still guards) — REUSING the whole engine (binding chain, async poll, sink);
# marks each applied. CLI: `generate [--name]` + `migrate`. ProvisionApp gained optional `migrations`. WITNESSED —
# provision 37 pass: diffSnapshots (empty->creates DAG-ordered, update, deprovision, unchanged->none); generate
# (0000/no-op-null/0001-delta-only); migrate (pending-only + idempotent re-run + the add-then-drop lifecycle via the
# engine, binding chain intact); fileMigrationStore round-trips across a fresh store over the same dir; the CLI
# generate/migrate/up-to-date + no-store->exit2. tsc clean. The provision package now offers BOTH the direct
# (plan/apply/push) AND the repeatable-documentable (generate/migrate + snapshots) paths. REMAINING: the stripe broker +
# the toolfactory cutover (replace provision.ts/provision-kv/provision-domains/mint-*/sync-secrets with a provision.config
# + a committed migration history).
claim provision_snapshot_migration_model_built: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when provision_snapshot_migration_model_built == False
